+## DramaQA sub-question extension (local LBA preservation branch)
+
+The `local/flipped-vqa-workspace` branch adds DramaQA Questioner and
+sub-question datasets to the upstream Flipped-VQA code. Its inputs remain
+external: `data/dramaqa/AnotherMissOhQA_{train,val,test}_set.json` and
+`data/dramaqa/clipvitl14.pth`.
+
+The training scripts use these checkpoints and output directories:
+
+| Script | Purpose | Output or checkpoint |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `dramaqa.sh` | Train the DramaQA baseline | `checkpoint/dramaqa/checkpoint_best.pth` |
+| `subqa_dramaqa_singlegpu.sh` | Train on the sub-question dataset with one GPU | `checkpoint/subqa_dramaqa/` |
+| `subqa_dramaqa_multigpu.sh` | Train on the sub-question dataset with six GPUs | `checkpoint/subqa_dramaqa/` |
+| `test_subqa_dramaqa_multigpu.sh` | Evaluate the saved sub-question checkpoint | `checkpoint/subqa_dramaqa/checkpoint_best.pth` |
+
+Run the baseline before either sub-question training script. The multi-GPU
+scripts currently select devices `0,1,2,3,4,5`; adjust `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`
+and `--nproc_per_node` together for a different worker count. The fork's
+existing `master` branch is unchanged; this extension is kept on the separate
+LBA preservation branch.
+
 ## Training LLaMA-VQA (LLaMA + Flipped-VQA)
 
